                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "774900de-093b-3336-bff9-b1fd0f15ae17",
                        "entry_id": "96d13f9d-72e2-3871-bde5-afe2ba57ee80",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An epithet of the Roman goddess Juno or (less often) Diana in the role of goddess of childbirth, midwives, and newborns."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "23d50d34-7aff-4c4c-bf23-4608069e6977",
                                "sense_id": "774900de-093b-3336-bff9-b1fd0f15ae17",
                                "text": "Lucina, the Sabine goddess of light, was combined with the Roman Juno, and as Juno Lucina, goddess of childbirth, she brought children into the world."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bc0147e5-a932-3087-8fbf-f8821585f2d1",
                        "entry_id": "96d13f9d-72e2-3871-bde5-afe2ba57ee80",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A separate goddess of those fields, a daughter of Jupiter and Juno and counterpart to the Greek Eileithyia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4093b8e-e290-4b9d-ae14-972f109983ec",
                                "sense_id": "bc0147e5-a932-3087-8fbf-f8821585f2d1",
                                "text": "Many believe the genesis of saint Lucy can be found in the mythology of two roman deities: Lucina, goddess of birth and light, who merged with the mother goddess Juno."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b50c6ba-28a0-40ff-a608-5083e8d8470f",
                                "sense_id": "bc0147e5-a932-3087-8fbf-f8821585f2d1",
                                "text": "2014, Alison Findlay, birth, entry in Women in Shakespeare: A Dictionary, unnumbered page,\nHe can only pray to Lucina, goddess of childbirth and 'gentle midwife/ To those that cry at night' to speed Thaisa's delivery (Per. 3.1.10–14), and has not even time to commit her body to the sea during the storm."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73155f8d-47f8-34d8-8e08-84bb0ab767fc",
                        "entry_id": "96d13f9d-72e2-3871-bde5-afe2ba57ee80",
                        "glosses": [
                            "146 Lucina, a Main Belt asteroid."
